The implementation of `logic.cjs` has been repaired to correctly merge overlapping and touching maintenance windows, as well as to handle negative endpoints and discard empty or reversed windows. A new regression test file `regression_test.cjs` has been added to verify the logic against various edge cases, including the example provided in the `README.md`.

The public tests and the new regression tests have both been executed successfully.

**Verification Results:**

- **Public Tests (`node public_test.cjs`):** Passed.
- **Regression Tests (`node regression_test.cjs`):** Passed.

**Final Implementation of `logic.cjs`:**

```javascript
exports.solve = function(x) {
  const windows = x.windows || [];
  const sorted = windows
    .filter(([a, b]) => a < b)
    .sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);

  const result = [];
  for (const window of sorted) {
    if (result.length === 0) {
      result.push([...window]);
    } else {
      const last = result[result.length - 1];
      if (window[0] <= last[1]) {
        last[1] = Math.max(last[1], window[1]);
      } else {
        result.push([...window]);
      }
    }
  }
  return result;
};
```

